        "title_top": "",
        "title": "Expert Backed Review Summary",
        "text": "<p>The RENPHO 4D Red Light Therapy Mask stands out for its combination of flexibility, coverage, and targeted wavelengths. Its 324 LED array delivers three treatment modes: red light (630nm) paired with near-infrared light (850nm) to support collagen production and improve the appearance of fine lines, blue light (415–470nm) to help manage mild inflammatory acne, and a mixed-light mode that combines all wavelengths for overall skin rejuvenation. The soft silicone design contours closely to the face, including the chin and jawline—areas often overlooked by rigid LED masks. Red light therapy, also known as photobiomodulation, has been studied for its ability to stimulate fibroblast activity and support skin repair when used consistently over time. However, results are gradual rather than immediate. Most users who notice improvements in skin texture, radiance, or breakouts report doing so after several weeks of regular use. It's also important to recognize that at-home LED masks are designed for mild to moderate concerns and shouldn't be viewed as replacements for in-office dermatological procedures. Individuals with photosensitivity disorders or those taking light-sensitizing medications should consult a healthcare professional before use.</p>",
        "body_align": "center",
        "content_width": "narrow",
